astSimplify did not replace a GrismMap followed by its own inverse with a UnitMap, and did replace a GrismMap followed by the inverse of one of a different order (GrismM), although that pair is not a unit transformation. Both are fixed. A GrismMap is now canceled only by the inverse of a GrismMap that describes the same grism to within a relative tolerance, so two whose reference wavelengths differ by less than 1e-12 m are no longer taken to be the same. It is not canceled if it has no dispersion, or if its reference ray is not diffracted, since the pair then gives a bad value for every input.
